criptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-04-20T12:40:15Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/1103952621","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/10204#issuecomment-1103952621","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/10204","id":1103952621,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAT2ozs5BzPrt","user":{"login":"andrewlewis","id":107897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzg5Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis","html_url":"https://github.com/andrewlewis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-20T13:46:15Z","updated_at":"2022-04-20T13:46:15Z","body":"If this is for plain DTS it looks like it only goes up to 5.1 so we could conservatively check for 6 channel output capability. That should be safe in the sense that there can't be more channels in the stream when it loads. For HDMI audio capabilities we get a max channel count so that probably means that fewer channels than the max are always supported.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/1103952621/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"andrewlewis","id":107897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzg5Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis","html_url":"https://github.com/andrewlewis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/1110443504","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/10204#issuecomment-1110443504","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/10204","id":1110443504,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAT2ozs5CMAXw","user":{"login":"cedricxperi","id":90685789,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNjg1Nzg5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90685789?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi","html_url":"https://github.com/cedricxperi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-27T01:50:07Z","updated_at":"2022-04-27T01:55:06Z","body":"Hi @andrewlewis @christosts ,\r\n\r\nPicking up on your suggestions, how about something like below in DefaultAudioSink.getEncodingAndChannelConfigForPassthrough(). I have tested that the below works for passing through DTS Digital surround on Nvidia Shield TV Pro. Thanks.\r\n\r\nif (encoding == C.ENCODING_E_AC3_JOC) {\r\n      // E-AC3 JOC is object based so the format channel count is arbitrary. From API 29 we can get\r\n      // the channel count for this encoding, but before then there is no way to query it so we\r\n      // assume 6 channel audio is supported.\r\n      if (Util.SDK_INT >= 29) {\r\n        // Default to 48 kHz if the format doesn't have a sample rate (for example, for chunkless\r\n        // HLS preparation). See [Internal: b/222127949].\r\n        int sampleRate = format.sampleRate != NO_VALUE ? format.sampleRate : 48000;\r\n        channelCount =\r\n            getMaxSupportedChannelCountForPassthroughV29(C.ENCODING_E_AC3_JOC, sampleRate);\r\n        if (channelCount == 0) {\r\n          Log.w(TAG, \"E-AC3 JOC encoding supported but no channel count supported\");\r\n          return null;\r\n        }\r\n      } else {\r\n        channelCount = 6;\r\n      }\r\n    } **_else if (encoding == C.ENCODING_DTS) {\r\n      channelCount = format.channelCount;\r\n      if (channelCount == NO_VALUE){\r\n        channelCount = 6;\r\n      }\r\n    } else {_**\r\n      channelCount = format.channelCount;\r\n      if (channelCount > audioCapabilities.getMaxChannelCount()) {\r\n        return null;\r\n      }\r\n    }","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/1110443504/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"cedricxperi","id":90685789,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNjg1Nzg5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90685789?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi","html_url":"https://github.com/cedricxperi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cedricxperi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":6503110584,"node_id":"MEE_lADOAT2ozs5IELQzzwAAAAGDnZe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/events/6503110584","actor":{"login":"andrewlewis","id":107897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzg5Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/us